Minato's patch to frameworks/base's core/java/android/text/util/Linkify.java at android-15.0.0_r1 (Apache-2.0), services
batch B: the tel: URL of a phone number that libphonenumber found.

Why: Linkify makes the URL with PhoneNumberUtils.normalizeNumber, and android.telephony.PhoneNumberUtils would need
hidden telephony properties, TelephonyManager members and flags that no step takes (11 compile errors). The patch gives
Linkify a private normalizeNumber with the same work for what libphonenumber matches (digits of any script, a leading
plus, a letter as its keypad digit), so Linkify.addLinks(PHONE_NUMBERS) and TextView's autoLink make the same links as
Android's without taking PhoneNumberUtils.

tools/build-framework.sh applies it to a copy in build/framework/src, never to build/sources.

--- a/core/java/android/text/util/Linkify.java
+++ b/core/java/android/text/util/Linkify.java
@@ -686,13 +686,34 @@
                 regionCode, Leniency.POSSIBLE, Long.MAX_VALUE);
         for (PhoneNumberMatch match : matches) {
             LinkSpec spec = new LinkSpec();
-            spec.url = "tel:" + PhoneNumberUtils.normalizeNumber(match.rawString());
+            spec.url = "tel:" + normalizeNumber(match.rawString());
             spec.start = match.start();
             spec.end = match.end();
             links.add(spec);
         }
     }
 
+    /**
+     * PhoneNumberUtils.normalizeNumber's work for a number libphonenumber found: its digits (any script), a leading
+     * plus, and a letter as the digit of its key on a phone's keypad. Minato does not take PhoneNumberUtils, whose
+     * telephony properties and flags no step has.
+     */
+    private static String normalizeNumber(String number) {
+        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
+        for (int i = 0; i < number.length(); i++) {
+            char c = number.charAt(i);
+            int digit = Character.digit(c, 10);
+            if (digit != -1) {
+                sb.append(digit);
+            } else if (i == 0 && c == '+') {
+                sb.append(c);
+            } else if ((c >= 'a' && c <= 'z') || (c >= 'A' && c <= 'Z')) {
+                sb.append("22233344455566677778889999".charAt(Character.toLowerCase(c) - 'a'));
+            }
+        }
+        return sb.toString();
+    }
+
